                                       |      
                                      ( )     

Hittite nouns were sometimes written with a special sign in front, called a
"determinative". These weren't pronounced, but indicated something about the
noun, like how "amber" is a rock but "Amber" is a person. GIŠ, for example,
marks that something is made of wood.

